I don't know how I missed this quaint little detail up until now, but
apparently *nothing* will distract our little NetHack pals while
they're engraving with a gem.

I was engraving "polymorphpolymorphpolymorph" adjacent to a boulder
covering a polymorph trap on DL9 of the mines, as I have a bad habit
of forgetting about boulders covering things and instinctively pushing
them around.  Anyway, a yeti came up and slowly beat my level 13
Tourist to death as he obsessively continued his creative writing
project.  I made an additional stupidity contribution to this death: I
see now that I'd forgotten to put half my bloody armour, including my
[CoD, back on after an intentional romantic interlude with a succubus,
and would undoubtedly have survived this encounter otherwise...

This was all *after* I fell through a trap door as an XL9 Tourist,
encountered a master lich generated by this same polymorph trap on the
way back up, made use of one of the few identified things in my
inventory, a /WoDigging, to escape from his summoned pals, and was
*very* lucky to find a cockatrice a couple levels down to come finish
him and his nasties off.

This was a promising Tourist, too.  He had [GoP from a minetown
fountain wish (very fortunate as he had a little strength=9 problem of
his own making), a [CoD from a minetown shop, was a dart Expert, and
was working with a +3 Mjollnir as his third sacrifice artifact (the
first two were Cleaver and Dragonbane).

